# i18n — Romanian & Russian

The app has two locales: **`ro`** (Romanian) and **`ru`** (Russian). Every user-facing string must support both from day one.

## Rules

- Never hardcode UI copy in components (labels, buttons, errors, empty states, toasts, placeholders, confirmations)
- Add keys to **both** `ro` and `ru` locale files in the same change
- Domain/content fields that are language-specific (name, URL, SEO, ALT, FAQ, descriptions) are modeled as `{ ro: string; ru: string }` (or equivalent), not a single string
- Default / primary catalog language follows product docs; admin UI must switch between `ro` and `ru`
- Key naming: `feature.section.key` (e.g. `categories.form.name`, `common.save`)
- Keep translations in `shared/i18n` (or equivalent); presentation only consumes `t('...')`

## ❌ BAD

```tsx
<Button>Сохранить</Button>
<input placeholder="Название категории" />
```

## ✅ GOOD

```tsx
<Button>{t('common.save')}</Button>
<Input placeholder={t('categories.form.namePlaceholder')} />
// locales/ro.json + locales/ru.json both updated
```
